# Times are America/Denver (TZ is set in the container), so DST is handled automatically.
# Job 1: pull the OptionStrat data and list the tickers for equity-watch's beta job.
45 7  * * 1-5  /app/fetch.sh
25 13 * * 1-5  /app/fetch.sh
# Job 2: build and publish the report from that data. In the morning equity-watch runs its beta job
# at 08:05 (about a minute at its throttled rate), so 08:10 follows it by a few minutes; if either
# moves, move the other, and keep the gap under report.sh's 90-minute limit. The afternoon run follows
# the 13:25 fetch straight away, so the page is up with time to act before the 14:00 close. It uses the
# morning's betas (good for betaMaxAgeDays); waiting for equity-watch's 14:05 job would land after the close.
10 8  * * 1-5  /app/publish.sh
27 13 * * 1-5  /app/publish.sh
# Paper trades (paper.js), kept apart from the real book in reports/paper/. check fills resting profit targets
# from live quotes every 15 minutes through the session (7:30 to 14:00 here; it does nothing outside it, or
# with no open paper trades). snapshot marks the paper book just before each publish, which uploads it; the
# morning one after equity-watch's beta job (08:05, about a minute), which fetch.sh gives the paper symbols too.
*/15 7-13 * * 1-5  cd /app && node paper.js check
8 8  * * 1-5  cd /app && node paper.js snapshot
26 13 * * 1-5  cd /app && node paper.js snapshot
